{
  "schema": "melusina.store.vendor-provenance.v1",
  "comment": [
    "vendor/ holds four modules of the Melusina monorepo, which go.mod replaces with ../../../Melusina/shared/<module>. Every",
    "release build passes -mod=vendor, so the Store compiles these vendored files and never reads a Melusina checkout. This file",
    "names the one Melusina commit the vendored files were exported from, the tree id of each module at that commit, and the",
    "blob id of every file go mod vendor wrote. Do not edit a vendored file: a change goes to Melusina main first.",
    "vendor_provenance_test.go checks on every run, without a Melusina clone: each object in git-objects/ hashes to its file",
    "name; the walk from sourceCommit through those trees reaches each module's tree and each recorded blob; every file under",
    "vendor/<module>/ is a recorded file with that blob, and none is missing; no vendored file is one go mod vendor never",
    "writes (_test.go, go.mod, go.sum, testdata/); and go.mod and vendor/modules.txt replace exactly these modules with",
    "exactly these paths. An auditor with a Melusina clone checks the rest in one command per module:",
    "  git -C <clone> rev-parse <sourceCommit>:<sourcePath>   must print the module's tree",
    "  git -C <clone> merge-base --is-ancestor <sourceCommit> origin/main",
    "To re-vendor from a newer Melusina main commit C:",
    "  1. export the four modules to a directory R: git -C <clone> archive C shared/melusina-attest",
    "     shared/melusina-identity-gate shared/melusina-artifact-vault shared/melusina-solana-primitives | tar -x -C R/Melusina",
    "  2. reach this module through a path whose ../../../Melusina is R/Melusina (for example a symlink R/store to the Store",
    "     checkout, entered as R/store/sidecar/melusina-store-sidecar) and run GOFLAGS= GOWORK=off go mod vendor there.",
    "     Leave go.mod's replace lines as they are: each binary's build info records them, so a new path changes the bytes.",
    "  3. set sourceCommit, each module's tree and every file's blob from C, and replace git-objects/ with C's commit object",
    "     (git cat-file commit C) and the trees on the walk to each vendored file (git cat-file tree <id>). The test names",
    "     each object it is missing."
  ],
